## Chapter 8 Checks of the Higher Moments Analysis

This is the first time a systematic analysis of the moments of the \(\left\langle p_{\mathrm{t}}\right\rangle\) spectra has been attempted. A detailed study of the effects of the analysis cuts and detector efficiency on the moments and cumulant ratios was undertaken. In Section 8.1 the effect of both the width and symmetry of the \(\eta\) cut is studied, in Section 8.2 the effect of the upper \(p_{\mathrm{t}}\) cut is studied, and in Section 8.3 the effect of \(p_{\mathrm{t}}\) dependent efficiency is studied. Additionally, in Section 8.4 the method used for calculating the errors of the moments and cumulant ratios is presented, and the systematic error of the higher moments analyses is estimated.

